upx_packed_pe_arm64.exe -- a win64/arm64 UPX image, the target `kuna unpack`
names as unsupported rather than rebuilding.

What it is
  A MinGW-w64 (llvm-mingw) AArch64 "hello" console program packed by UPX 5.3.0,
  the first release with the win64/arm64 target. 7,168 bytes packed; 9,728
  unpacked. PackHeader at 0x1fd: version=13, format=43 (win64/arm64), method=2,
  filter=0x52.

  The trailer layout is the PE32+ one kuna rebuilds for win64/pe, but the code is
  filtered with ARM64 branch tricks (0x52 under the code's bias, or the new 0x53)
  that kuna does not reverse, so the unpacker refuses the target by name and
  writes nothing; the test pins that.

Where it came from
  Built in the mstorsjo/llvm-mingw docker image (clang 23.1.4):

      aarch64-w64-mingw32-clang -O1 -s -o hello_arm64.exe hello.c    # puts("hello")
      upx -o upx_packed_pe_arm64.exe hello_arm64.exe                 # UPX 5.3.0

  sha256(original)  0b31c95f9a1c69efacf260e7a60155431cd94934de9b0c7ca62c33db163d150a
  sha256(packed)    384ad2c827bc8a6aaa7babed9090a38a037e9b89b055786c74b9047bbf9efe3a

Why it is vendored rather than built
  `upx` is not installed on CI, and neither is a MinGW toolchain.
